      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://www.stselectronicrecyclinginc.com/bakersfield-ca#faqpage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What certifications and standards do you reference?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "STS Electronic Recycling references NIST SP 800-88 guidelines for media sanitization across all engagements. Under these guidelines, media sanitization requires verification of purge-level overwrite or physical destruction. This approach supports organizations needing documented processes for sensitive data. The sts-hq-callout above details where equipment collected in Bakersfield is processed. We focus on transparent, documented handling that supports compliance efforts for energy, agriculture, healthcare, and education clients throughout Kern County. For healthcare clients, processes are designed to support HIPAA technical safeguards through chain-of-custody records and serial-level certificates. California enforces strict universal waste rules under the Electronic Waste Recycling Act. STS services help businesses meet these expectations with accurate reporting from pickup through final material recovery at our processing operation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you serve?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We serve Bakersfield and throughout Kern County including energy corridors along Highway 58 and Interstate 5, agricultural operations, healthcare facilities, educational campuses, and logistics hubs. Pickup is scheduled based on volume and location within the greater Kern County region. Organizations searching for electronics recycling near me in Bakersfield and surrounding communities find STS provides reliable service with documented chain of custody from collection through final processing."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is pickup really free?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Pickup is provided at no additional charge for qualifying volumes. Contact our team at (844) 699-2913 to determine eligibility based on your specific equipment mix and location in the Bakersfield or Kern County area. STS engagements with commercial clients in energy and agriculture typically qualify for complimentary scheduled pickup when minimum volume thresholds are met. This approach supports sustainable operations while maintaining full documentation for audit and compliance purposes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do you support HIPAA requirements?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For healthcare clients including Kern Medical and Adventist Health Bakersfield, our processes are designed to support HIPAA technical safeguards through documented sanitization and chain-of-custody records. NIST SP 800-88 guidelines inform the destruction methods used. STS engagements with healthcare systems typically coordinate off-hours pickups to minimize disruption to patient care. Services help organizations prepare documentation for audits but do not guarantee regulatory outcomes. Equipment collected in Bakersfield is transported to our certified processing facilities in Jacksonville and Houston, Texas for final handling. According to the UN Global E-waste Monitor, only a small percentage of global electronic waste is processed responsibly. STS contributes to responsible material recovery with transparent reporting that tracks every asset from Kern County pickup through final disposition. This level of documentation supports compliance officers responsible for protected health information safeguards across Kern County healthcare networks."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer on-site hard drive destruction in Bakersfield?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS provides on-site hard drive destruction and mobile shredding services for Bakersfield organizations with high-security requirements. Witnessed destruction, video documentation, and immediate certificates of destruction are available for healthcare, financial, and government clients in Kern County."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What happens to equipment after pickup in Kern County?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Equipment collected in Bakersfield and Kern County is transported under continuous chain-of-custody documentation to one of our two certified processing facilities in Jacksonville, Texas or Houston, Texas. There it undergoes NIST 800-88 compliant data sanitization, material separation, and responsible downstream processing with zero landfill commitment. Full reporting is provided to the customer."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you handle large enterprise ITAD projects for energy companies?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. STS regularly manages large-scale ITAD projects for California energy operators and agricultural producers in the San Joaquin Valley. Our 200,000 sq ft processing operation, secure fleet, and experienced project managers allow us to coordinate multi-site collections with minimal operational disruption while maintaining full compliance documentation."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide certificates of destruction for regulatory audits?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Every engagement includes a detailed certificate of destruction listing serial numbers (where available), destruction method, weight, date, and downstream facility information. These certificates are designed to support HIPAA, NIST, SOX, GLBA, and California regulatory audit requirements for Bakersfield and Kern County organizations."
          }
        }
      ]
